-covered 19  baseline levels  which was 47.4 and 29.3  respectively this equates to an increase  in the average number of days doing 30  minutes of physical exercise  from 3.8 days to 4.1 days  however the proportion who reported  being physically  active decreased over the first two  weeks of the survey  from 62.2 week commencing the 13th of  april  to 55.5 percent week commencing the 20th  of april  this data was extracted from the essex  county council's state of life survey  initial highlights report prevalence of  long-term conditions  quality outcome framework also known as  quaff prevalence is the estimated  proportion of all those registered at gp  surgeries  with a diagnosis it tells us how common  certain conditions are in a particular  area  diabetes quaff prevalence for people age  17 plus is given for the castle point  and rockford ccg  area combined prevalence of hypertension  coronary heart disease  stroke and dementia is fairly similar in  carter point and rockford  although hypertension is slightly higher  in castle point  at 18.07 percent than rochford at 16.13  and dementia is slightly higher in  rochford at 1.04  than in castle point at 0.77 percent  the quaff prevalence of all conditions  is higher than the essex and england  averages for each  these figures were obtained from the  jsna 2019 profiles  emergency hospital admissions the number  of emergency hospital admissions due to  hip fractures  stroke and coronary heart disease are  fairly similar in castle point and  rockford  but emergency hospital admission is due  to chronic obstructive pulmonary disease  are much higher in castle point than in  rochford  in castle point there are 102 compared  to 81.6  in rockford the emergency admission  ratio for copd in castle  point is 102 and in rockford is 81.6  the emergency admission ratio for chd in  castle point  is 84.7 and in rockford is 90.5  the emergency admission ratio for hip  fractures in castle point  is 104.5 and in rockford is 101.9 